# Mild-R Fanclub Website — Cursor Rules

You are assisting on a high-quality VTuber Fanclub website for **Mild-R** (World End / Lumina Project), featuring scrollytelling and parallax effects.

## Confirmation-First Workflow (STRICT)

1. NEVER create, modify, or delete any files immediately on your own.
2. Before taking any action, ALWAYS outline what you are going to do and ask for confirmation.
3. WAIT for the user to reply with confirmation words in Thai such as: **「ตกลง」**, **「ทำเลย」**, **「ยืนยัน」**, **「เริ่ม」**, or similar, before executing code or generating files.
4. Apply these rules for the entire duration of this project — every step, every file change.

## Tech Stack (STRICT — Do Not Substitute)

Whenever writing code or suggesting installations, use ONLY this stack. Do NOT suggest Material UI, Bootstrap, Framer Motion, or other alternatives:

1. **Framework:** Next.js (App Router) with TypeScript
2. **Styling:** Tailwind CSS
3. **Animations:** GSAP — specifically ScrollTrigger and `@gsap/react` for all scrollytelling and parallax
4. **UI Components:** shadcn/ui (Buttons, Dialogs, Cards, etc.) — Tailwind-based, customizable, GSAP-friendly
5. **Icons:** lucide-react

## Library-First Policy

1. Before building a non-trivial feature (image crop, QR, date picker,
   drag & drop, carousel, etc.), look for a well-maintained library first.
   Do not hand-roll it unless necessary.
2. Hand-rolling is allowed only when no suitable library exists, the library
   conflicts with the Tech Stack (e.g. animation libraries other than GSAP,
   UI kits other than shadcn/ui), or the code is only a few lines.
3. When proposing a library, state: name, exact version (released at least
   2 weeks ago), license, last release / maintenance, React 19 compatibility,
   and why it beats hand-rolling. Wait for approval before installing.
4. Pin exact versions in package.json.

The Tech Stack rule above still applies: a library must not replace any part of
that stack (no Material UI, Bootstrap, Framer Motion, etc.).

## Project Focus

- Mild-R profile, lore, and related fanclub content
- Scrollytelling + layered parallax (transparent PNGs)
- Clean folder structure optimized for animation layers and section components

## Project Images (STRICT)

- NEVER feed any project image into AI image generation or editing.
- NEVER use project images for anything else (designs, uploads, code) without explicit permission from the user.
- Exception: converting file format and reducing file size are allowed without asking.
